# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Your full-resolution originals.
#
# These are NOT uploaded to GitHub. They are large, and hundreds of
# them would eventually make the repository slow and unwieldy.
#
# THIS MEANS GITHUB IS NOT BACKING UP YOUR ORIGINALS.
# Keep your own copy somewhere else - an external drive, Google
# Drive, iCloud, Dropbox, anything. If this computer dies, the
# web-sized photos survive on GitHub but the originals do not.
#
# If you would rather have them backed up on GitHub anyway, delete
# the single line below. Fine for a few hundred photos.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
photo-originals/

# Windows / macOS clutter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS. These never go to GitHub.
#
# discord-bot.secret.json holds the password for your Discord bot.
# This repository is PUBLIC. Anyone who reads that token could read
# every message in your Discord server.
#
# If it ever does get uploaded, or you paste it anywhere by mistake:
# go to discord.com/developers, open your app, click Bot, click
# Reset Token. The old one stops working immediately.
#
# The glob is deliberate - renaming the file must not un-hide it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
*.secret.json
*.secret
discord-bot.secret.json

# Which Discord messages have already been imported. Local bookkeeping,
# not worth uploading, and it names your channels.
.import-state.json
tools/.import-state.json
